---
/*
 * Identity resolution as a graph, which is the one idea in this case study that
 * prose cannot carry: record 1 and record 2 share a phone, record 2 and record 3
 * share an email, so all three are one person even though 1 and 3 have nothing
 * in common. Union-Find collapses the component to one representative.
 *
 * Inline SVG, no library, no external request. Records are numbered, never named,
 * and no source system appears: the anonymisation rule holds inside the diagram
 * as much as it does in the copy.
 */
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 560 200"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="idgraph-title idgraph-desc"
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  >
    <title id="idgraph-title">Three customer records resolved to one golden ID</title>
    <desc id="idgraph-desc">
      Record 1 and record 2 are joined by a shared name and phone number. Record 2 and record 3 are
      joined by a shared name and email address. Records 1 and 3 share nothing directly. Connected
      components collapses all three into a single golden ID.
    </desc>

    <!-- Edges first, so the node fills cover the line ends. -->
    <g class="edge">
      <line x1="64" y1="74" x2="184" y2="158" />
      <line x1="184" y1="158" x2="304" y2="74" />
    </g>

    <!-- No edge between 1 and 3. That is the whole point, so absence is drawn. -->
    <g class="edge is-absent">
      <line x1="73" y1="74" x2="295" y2="74" />
    </g>

    <g class="node">
      <circle cx="64" cy="74" r="9" />
      <circle cx="184" cy="158" r="9" />
      <circle cx="304" cy="74" r="9" />
    </g>

    <g class="node-label">
      <text x="64" y="42" text-anchor="middle">record 1</text>
      <text x="304" y="42" text-anchor="middle">record 3</text>
      <text x="184" y="186" text-anchor="middle">record 2</text>
    </g>

    <g class="edge-label">
      <text x="184" y="64" text-anchor="middle">nothing in common</text>
      <text x="112" y="116" text-anchor="end">name + phone</text>
      <text x="264" y="116">name + email</text>
    </g>

    <g class="collapse">
      <line x1="372" y1="116" x2="432" y2="116" />
      <polygon points="432,110 446,116 432,122" />
      <text x="409" y="104" text-anchor="middle">union-find</text>
    </g>

    <g class="accent">
      <circle cx="486" cy="116" r="15" />
      <text x="486" y="158" text-anchor="middle">one golden ID</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <figcaption>
    Record 1 shares a name and phone with record 2, record 2 shares a name and email with record 3,
    and records 1 and 3 share nothing. All three are the same person, so connected components
    resolves them to one golden ID.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

